# How many times richer is the richest country than the poorest?
subtitle: "Guess how many times richer the richest country is than the poorest, then see the gap in coins, and how small it was in 1820."
tags: ["economics","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Guess the gap\" note \"Richest vs poorest\""

## How many times richer is the richest country than the poorest?
sources:
    - id: owid_gdp
      title: GDP per capita
      authors: Our World in Data, from the World Bank, Eurostat, OECD and IMF
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/gdp-per-capita-worldbank
      finding: 'GDP per person in 2025, in 2021 international dollars (adjusted for prices): Singapore about $139,600, the highest; Burundi about $1,070, the lowest; about 131 times apart'
    - id: owid_mad
      title: GDP per capita, 1820 to today (Maddison Project Database)
      authors: Our World in Data, from the Maddison Project Database (Bolt and van Zanden)
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/gdp-per-capita-maddison-project-database
      finding: '1820: United Kingdom $3,306 (highest of 54 countries), Nepal $641 (lowest), about 5 times; 2022: the poorest, Central African Republic, $596'

